{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play","id":834478,"title":"[2e] Making the Seasonal Courts for Actual Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-21T10:12:35-08:00","id":834478,"title":"[2e] Making the Seasonal Courts for Actual Play","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> My group will be trying out 2e content with existing characters. Since we are already in the seasonal courts, we would like to stick with that.<br /> <br /> What would you guys do for the Mantle Benefits in 2e?<br /> <br /> What does a universal contract being &quot;in court&quot; mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:26:58-08:00","id":834488,"title":"","content":"If you can wait until release, they'll get an update along with Miami in the new book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:33:43-08:00","id":834491,"title":"","content":"I think that the Court Contract is made as a Goblin Vow and granted at Court Mantle 2, if I understand the way the system works. I don't know if every changeling gets the same benefit because of the original founder, or if it each changeling gets to make a specific Goblin Vow with an aspect of the Court's purview. I also don't know if the Mantle benefits are fixed or each changeling picks something they want that is thematic with the Court. I'd really appreciate clarification on that.<br /> <br /> My take (assuming the benefits are fixed) would be something like this.<br /> <br /> Spring:<br /> \u2022 Striking Looks 1.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 9-again in Persuasion.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Three dots of Staff (smitten admirers), Contacts or Truefriend, changeling's choice.<br /> <br /> Summer:<br /> \u2022 +1 to Weaponry, Firearms, Brawl or Athletics when attacking an enemy of the Freehold.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 to Initiative.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 Health.<br /> <br /> Autumn:<br /> \u2022 Others take a -1 to influence the Autumn Courtiers' dreams.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 9-again in Intimidate.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gains Rote to Occult rolls.<br /> <br /> Winter:<br /> \u2022 +1 to Stealth and Subterfuge vs. creatures connected to the Wyrd.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 to Defence.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Three dots of Closed Book and immunity to normal cold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:22:04-08:00","id":834510,"title":"","content":"For now just use the Toronto Courts, but subsititute the Seasonal Courts themes and emotions.<br /> <br /> So for example use the Ivory Court for Spring, use the Ivory Court Mantle but change the symbols to that of the Spring Court and use the desire emotion instead of greed.<br /> <br /> Take the Court of Brass and use that mantle as Autumn, but changed the fluff to fear and Autumn and the emotion to fear.<br /> <br /> Take the Jade Court Mantle and change it to the Winter Court, make it about Cold and Sorrow instead of Pride.<br /> <br /> Take the Silver Court and make it into the Summer Court, its emotion is already wrath and its symbolism is a mix of the Seasonal Courts and the Seelie Courts, so it won't take much to change it to the Summer Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T11:23:15-08:00","id":834514,"title":"","content":"You can change it to the proper Seasonal Courts when that Changeling: The Lost 2e is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:12:52-08:00","id":834548,"title":"","content":"If we waited until the book was properly released, then We wouldn't be participating in the preview/open playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:38:36-08:00","id":834669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834491#post834491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Court Contract is made as a Goblin Vow and granted at Court Mantle 2, if I understand the way the system works. I don't know if every changeling gets the same benefit because of the original founder, or if it each changeling gets to make a specific Goblin Vow with an aspect of the Court's purview. I also don't know if the Mantle benefits are fixed or each changeling picks something they want that is thematic with the Court. I'd really appreciate clarification on that.<br /> <br /> My take (assuming the benefits are fixed) would be something like this.<br /> <br /> Spring:<br /> \u2022 Striking Looks 1.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 9-again in Persuasion.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Three dots of Staff (smitten admirers), Contacts or Truefriend, changeling's choice.<br /> <br /> Summer:<br /> \u2022 +1 to Weaponry, Firearms, Brawl or Athletics when attacking an enemy of the Freehold.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 to Initiative.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 Health.<br /> <br /> Autumn:<br /> \u2022 Others take a -1 to influence the Autumn Courtiers' dreams.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 9-again in Intimidate.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gains Rote to Occult rolls.<br /> <br /> Winter:<br /> \u2022 +1 to Stealth and Subterfuge vs. creatures connected to the Wyrd.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 +1 to Defence.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Personal Approach.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Three dots of Closed Book and immunity to normal cold.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is good, you should use this till CtL 2e is released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T17:30:24-08:00","id":834716,"title":"","content":"I'll give ShadowKnight my thumbs up. I'll be using those benefits for my seasonal courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T17:53:46-08:00","id":834727,"title":"","content":"What would you have as the target for Goblin Vow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T18:08:51-08:00","id":834732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834727#post834727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you have as the target for Goblin Vow?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't know if it's a universal thing for all courtiers or if each Changeling gets to make a different vow with a different aspect of the season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T18:45:41-08:00","id":834747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i> think that the Court Contract is made as a Goblin Vow</i> </div> </div> </div>What is this based on? According the Contract preview Court Contracts are still a thing.<br /> <br /> <b>edit</b>: Also, the premade courts have specific things for their 2 dot of mantle goblin vows, it doesn't seem to vary by changeling. For example Copper Court gets a dot of the Goblin Vow (mines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-21-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T19:35:29-08:00","id":834779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834747#post834747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is this based on? According the Contract preview Court Contracts are still a thing.<br /> <br /> <b>edit</b>: Also, the premade courts have specific things for their 2 dot of mantle goblin vows, it doesn't seem to vary by changeling. For example Copper Court gets a dot of the Goblin Vow (mines).</div> </div> </div> </div>The court writeup specifically says that at Mantle 2 you get a Goblin Vow, not a Court Contract. I think the mantle and the contract are separated (except perhaps a requirement to have as many mantle dots as you have court contract dots?).<br /> <br /> If it's specific, I'd probably go with Growth for Spring, Sun for Summer, Harvest for Autumn and Snow for Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T19:38:38-08:00","id":834782,"title":"","content":"If you wanted to be really simple, the Vow could quite easily just be with the specific season. Goblin Vow (Winter) is a pretty straightforward way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T19:45:14-08:00","id":834784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834779#post834779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The court writeup specifically says that at Mantle 2 you get a Goblin Vow, not a Court Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you get goblin vows from your second dot of mantle. I wasn't suggesting you get court contracts from mantle. I'm merely saying that Court Contracts are not made as goblin vows, since there is no indication to that as far as I'm aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T19:52:26-08:00","id":834791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834779#post834779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The court writeup specifically says that at Mantle 2 you get a Goblin Vow, not a Court Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Court Creation writeup also specifically states that membership in a Court gives you the Contracts of Talespinning, [Court's Emotion], and a third reflective of the Court's core theme and story. That's not a Goblin Vow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T20:17:03-08:00","id":834805,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess I got a bit mixed up on the different types of contracts, since we've only had universal conrracts and goblin vows spoiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:06:07-08:00","id":834952,"title":"","content":"If it helps, here are the working notes for my own setting. Note that it's a work in progress, and I haven't given the Court writeups that polished shine just yet. I'm trying to get everything worked out, <i>then</i> I can write up the history and everything. It's light on detail, but that might help you other players come up with ideas for your Freeholds.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><b>Court Contracts</b></u><br /> <b>Spring:</b><br /> Emotion (Desire)<br /> Fang and Talon \u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Probably going to change to Vainglory, but my initial reasoning was that the children of Spring were more closely tied with the birds and beasts, the living things growing upon the earth, especially in a place where nature is so prevalent. So they learn how to exult in Spring's glory the way the living creatures of Crescent Valley do. The valley is nestled right into the Cascade Mountains.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer:</b><br /> Emotion (Wrath)<br /> Might of the Terrible Brute \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn:</b><br /> Emotion (Fear)<br /> Night's Subtle Distractions \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Winter:</b><br /> Emotion (Sorrow)<br /> Touch of the Workman's Wrath \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <u><b>Mantles</b></u><br /> Each Court gains the following benefits at each level of Mantle.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022)</b><br /> Spring: Courtiers gain a keener awareness of the world and its delights. +2 to perception rolls.<br /> Summer: The anger of the Lost always simmers just beneath the surface. +2 to wrathful Intimidation rolls based on show of force.<br /> Autumn: Mysteries abound in Charleston's history. +2 when making research rolls pertaining to the occult.<br /> Winter: Gain +2 on Expression rolls made with members of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All: Gain a dot of the Goblin Vow Merit related to the Court.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Spring: Gain the Striking Looks (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Summer: Gain the Hardy (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Autumn: Gain the Eye for the Strange (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Winter: The cold, patient chill of Winter is a good time to stay indoors and study. You gain the Library (\u2022\u2022) Merit, choosing a Skill appropriate for the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All: Refine and prioritize a Court Approach. Huntsmen gain no benefit at all if they do not use this Approach first.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All Courtiers may choose Dual Kith (\u2022\u2022\u2022) at this level of Mantle instead of the below benefits.<br /> Spring: Your ability to immerse yourself in the healing energies of life grant you the Faerie Healing (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Summer: The mightiest of Summer are a powerful presence indeed. You gain the Enchanting Performance (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Autumn: You have tamed a powerful familiar to serve as ally and guardian. Gain the Hedgebeast Companion (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Winter: Your journeys into the snow-covered Hedge have given you command of a fae beast. You gain the Fae Mount (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Court Approaches</b></u><br /> <b>Spring</b><br /> <b>Beware the Roseflame:</b> An extremely rare flower, the Blue Roseflame, grows in the Hedge only during Spring. The flower is said to have intense aphrodisiacal qualities, and it never wilts as long as it is &quot;fed&quot; with Glamour. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they use the allure of the rare flower to bait changelings into a trap.<br /> <b>Dream Girl:</b> Despite its name, the Huntsman can appear in any form: male, female, androgynous, transgender, bearing whatever qualities a Spring courtier desires most. The Huntsman gains a point of Yearning if it seduces an otherwise wary changeling in exchange for another changeling's stolen desires.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b><br /> <b>Fire Pit Fight:</b> Summer courtiers in Charleston often wage ritual battles by firelight on hot summer nights out in Crescent Valley. If a Huntsman issues an earnest challenge to a changeling by the fire for its safety or something else precious, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <b>Quenching the Fire:</b> Summer never yields its anger. If a Huntsman can erode at the Summer courtier's sense of anger, whether by instilling joy or sorrow, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b><br /> <b>Theater of Dreams:</b> The Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they manipulate the dreams of a changeling's mortal allies in order to draw out the changeling.<br /> <b>Solemn Vow:</b> Huntsmen excel at twisting the bonds between the Lost. The Huntsman gains a point of Yearning if it can manipulate the changeling or one of her allies into breaking a pledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter</b><br /> <b>Not All Who Wander are Lost:</b> The Huntsmen are masters of manipulation. When one uses a token of something a changeling lost to break her confidence, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <b>Frozen Heart:</b> Winter courtiers are often wreathed in sorrow as the land is wreathed in snow and ice. If a Huntsman can prey upon a changeling's sorrow and convince her to retreat into mournful solitude, it gains a point of Yearning.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:19:15-08:00","id":834958,"title":"","content":"Do we actually know what contracts being a changelings affinity do anymore? If you pick a universal contract to be a courts contract what does that do? From the contract preview I had the impression you couldn't pick universal contracts for court affinity anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:00:00-08:00","id":834974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834958#post834958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we actually know what contracts being a changelings affinity do anymore? If you pick a universal contract to be a courts contract what does that do? From the contract preview I had the impression you couldn't pick universal contracts for court affinity anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when you make your character you get 5 dots of contracts and 2 of those dots have to be affinity. Affinity / universal contracts aren't really a thing anymore though, instead every contract has affinity to some number of seemings. When a seeming has affinity for a contract they will get a special power on top of the effects of the contract, other changelings can buy affinities for contracts they already own, but aren't tied to their seeming, at a cost of 1xp each though. Vainglory for example has 3 different affinities, a wizened one, a fairest one and a darkling on, so if you're a beast and buy vainglory you don't have any extra bonuses automatically when using vainglory, but you can spend 1xp to buy the fairest affinity and another 1xp to buy the wizened affinity for vainglory. If you're still confused I recommend reading the spoiled contracts rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:12:36-08:00","id":834980,"title":"","content":"Maybe the affinity contracts will get a special power based on the court. I could see a Winter Court with an affinity for Light-Shy with the added benefit of an exceptional roll with only 4 success and the possibility to substitute Wyrd for Mantle (Winter) on the dice roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:26:17-08:00","id":834986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834974#post834974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, when you make your character you get 5 dots of contracts and 2 of those dots have to be affinity. Affinity / universal contracts aren't really a thing anymore though, instead every contract has affinity to some number of seemings. When a seeming has affinity for a contract they will get a special power on top of the effects of the contract, other changelings can buy affinities for contracts they already own, but aren't tied to their seeming, at a cost of 1xp each though. Vainglory for example has 3 different affinities, a wizened one, a fairest one and a darkling on, so if you're a beast and buy vainglory you don't have any extra bonuses automatically when using vainglory, but you can spend 1xp to buy the fairest affinity and another 1xp to buy the wizened affinity for vainglory. If you're still confused I recommend reading the spoiled contracts rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not talking about seeming affinity..... I am talking about Court based &quot;affinity&quot;. The spoiled contract rules are why I am pretty sure you cannot have Court affinity with universal contract anymore, since Court Contracts are a seperate group and Contracts seem to all cost the same regardless of &quot;court affinity&quot; based on the XP cost rules found in the character creation rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T07:18:58-08:00","id":835025,"title":"","content":"One suggestion I've seen for Springs 5 dot mantle blessing that I think is really cool: Courtiers are so in tune with their desires that they may replenish a point of glamour any time they fulfill an aspiration. Once per story completing a significant long term aspiration refills their entire glamour pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:32:50-08:00","id":835587,"title":"","content":"The (to me) potentially awkward thing about 2E's Freehold and Court creation system is how every Freehold has its own unique Courts, which are now subgroups within each Freehold. Can you even have Court membership that spans multiple Freeholds, as 1E did? The existing Court document, which describes each Freehold as a unique story, with its Courts supporting that story, seems to indicate otherwise. Is the Winter Court of Freehold A separate from the Winter Court in Freehold B, even if they are mechanically identical? If not, do the Freeholds they support have to have identical stories, rituals, etc.? If they are separate, what happens when you leave Freehold A and join Freehold B? Do you lose your mantle and have to earn it all over again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:39:35-08:00","id":835590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=835587#post835587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Winter Court of Freehold A separate from the Winter Court in Freehold B, even if they are mechanically identical? If not, do the Freeholds they support have to have identical stories, rituals, etc.? If they are separate, what happens when you leave Freehold A and join Freehold B? Do you lose your mantle and have to earn it all over again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure no two Freeholds have identical stories and rituals.<br /> <br /> You probably lose your Court Mantle.<br /> <br /> As per Sanctity of Merits, you get the Mantle merit dots back, which you can apply towards a Mantle in the new Freehold if the ST is willing (and you put in the RPing effort).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:52:16-08:00","id":835595,"title":"","content":"Well...Ish.<br /> <br /> The fact of the matter is that there is form and function in the creation of the rituals that provide the metaphysical infrastructure for the Bulwark and the Courts, form and function that can be copied. The Seasonal Bulwark has been implied in the book to be the most prominent one in Western Europe, as an example, and that supposes that the ritual can be performed time and again with only minor deviance, if that.<br /> <br /> That said, Winter Masks has it's alternate Seasonal Courts for a reasons. Someone can deconstruct the rituals down and build them up as it best fits the needs of the area if they want to, to some degree.<br /> <br /> So the answer is No, there can be a spread of the same style of Freehold over a large area, and the Mantles from one can easily pass on from one to the other so long as the deviance of each freehold is not too much. But there is a little yes in there, as, well, yes, every freehold is going to individualize it a little bit.<br /> <br /> Or, even more simply, No, the Seasonal Courts do not only exist in Miami. That'd be a weird place for them to singularly exist anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T21:58:24-08:00","id":835599,"title":"","content":"I wonder if all of scotland would count as a single freehold for the purposes of their Seelie and Unseelie courts....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 02-23-2016, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T22:08:28-08:00","id":835605,"title":"","content":"Somehow, I rather severely doubt that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T23:02:18-08:00","id":835618,"title":"","content":"I am actually rather surprised that each Freehold doesn't have its own individual take on the Bulwark and its own variance on the rituals and court contracts, even if they have courts that have the same name and theme. I was especially expecting the Mantle benefits to be different as well, such as one Spring Court granting Striking Looks and another granting Contacts and yet another granting 9-again on Persuasion.<br /> <br /> It just feels like the sort of thing that would happen, you know? Each culture interprets the same symbols and stories in slightly different ways, and those differences can be significant enough to grant different mechanical bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T23:44:49-08:00","id":835626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=835618#post835618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am actually rather surprised that each Freehold doesn't have its own individual take on the Bulwark and its own variance on the rituals and court contracts, even if they have courts that have the same name and theme. I was especially expecting the Mantle benefits to be different as well, such as one Spring Court granting Striking Looks and another granting Contacts and yet another granting 9-again on Persuasion.<br /> <br /> It just feels like the sort of thing that would happen, you know? Each culture interprets the same symbols and stories in slightly different ways, and those differences can be significant enough to grant different mechanical bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that, in an ideal world, that would be the case but, asking people to come up with an entirely new set of everything is... a lot.<br /> <br /> For me, it's enough that the variation is encouraged but not required. You can toolbox it to exactly the level of creativity and effort you have available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T00:24:16-08:00","id":835629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=835605#post835605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somehow, I rather severely doubt that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there actually any restriction on how big a freehold can be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T10:19:47-08:00","id":835862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=835629#post835629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there actually any restriction on how big a freehold can be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> Also, apologies, last night I read it as Ireland rather than Scotland, and I felt like the political environment of that island just couldn't foster a unified freehold.<br /> <br /> Scotland could, maybe, though from how I understand it(Not very well), it has it's own divides.<br /> <br /> Still, be cool to see a country-wide freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T17:35:34-08:00","id":836121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=835862#post835862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not as I'm aware.<br /> <br /> Also, apologies, last night I read it as Ireland rather than Scotland, and I felt like the political environment of that island just couldn't foster a unified freehold.<br /> <br /> Scotland could, maybe, though from how I understand it(Not very well), it has it's own divides.<br /> <br /> Still, be cool to see a country-wide freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually my fault, I wrote Ireland first by mistake and then changed it to Scotland and then I made another edit after you made your post to use the correct &quot;their&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T00:23:15-08:00","id":836284,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see the Seelie and Unseelie courts written up. They're mentioned briefly in Toronto but has anyone done a fan version yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:13:04-08:00","id":836331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=834952#post834952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps, here are the working notes for my own setting. Note that it's a work in progress, and I haven't given the Court writeups that polished shine just yet. I'm trying to get everything worked out, <i>then</i> I can write up the history and everything. It's light on detail, but that might help you other players come up with ideas for your Freeholds.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u><b>Court Contracts</b></u><br /> <b>Spring:</b><br /> Emotion (Desire)<br /> Fang and Talon \u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Probably going to change to Vainglory, but my initial reasoning was that the children of Spring were more closely tied with the birds and beasts, the living things growing upon the earth, especially in a place where nature is so prevalent. So they learn how to exult in Spring's glory the way the living creatures of Crescent Valley do. The valley is nestled right into the Cascade Mountains.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer:</b><br /> Emotion (Wrath)<br /> Might of the Terrible Brute \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn:</b><br /> Emotion (Fear)<br /> Night's Subtle Distractions \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Winter:</b><br /> Emotion (Sorrow)<br /> Touch of the Workman's Wrath \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> <u><b>Mantles</b></u><br /> Each Court gains the following benefits at each level of Mantle.<br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022)</b><br /> Spring: Courtiers gain a keener awareness of the world and its delights. +2 to perception rolls.<br /> Summer: The anger of the Lost always simmers just beneath the surface. +2 to wrathful Intimidation rolls based on show of force.<br /> Autumn: Mysteries abound in Charleston's history. +2 when making research rolls pertaining to the occult.<br /> Winter: Gain +2 on Expression rolls made with members of the Freehold.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All: Gain a dot of the Goblin Vow Merit related to the Court.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Spring: Gain the Striking Looks (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Summer: Gain the Hardy (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Autumn: Gain the Eye for the Strange (\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Winter: The cold, patient chill of Winter is a good time to stay indoors and study. You gain the Library (\u2022\u2022) Merit, choosing a Skill appropriate for the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All: Refine and prioritize a Court Approach. Huntsmen gain no benefit at all if they do not use this Approach first.<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> All Courtiers may choose Dual Kith (\u2022\u2022\u2022) at this level of Mantle instead of the below benefits.<br /> Spring: Your ability to immerse yourself in the healing energies of life grant you the Faerie Healing (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Summer: The mightiest of Summer are a powerful presence indeed. You gain the Enchanting Performance (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Autumn: You have tamed a powerful familiar to serve as ally and guardian. Gain the Hedgebeast Companion (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> Winter: Your journeys into the snow-covered Hedge have given you command of a fae beast. You gain the Fae Mount (\u2022\u2022\u2022) Merit.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Court Approaches</b></u><br /> <b>Spring</b><br /> <b>Beware the Roseflame:</b> An extremely rare flower, the Blue Roseflame, grows in the Hedge only during Spring. The flower is said to have intense aphrodisiacal qualities, and it never wilts as long as it is &amp;quot;fed&amp;quot; with Glamour. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they use the allure of the rare flower to bait changelings into a trap.<br /> <b>Dream Girl:</b> Despite its name, the Huntsman can appear in any form: male, female, androgynous, transgender, bearing whatever qualities a Spring courtier desires most. The Huntsman gains a point of Yearning if it seduces an otherwise wary changeling in exchange for another changeling's stolen desires.<br /> <br /> <b>Summer</b><br /> <b>Fire Pit Fight:</b> Summer courtiers in Charleston often wage ritual battles by firelight on hot summer nights out in Crescent Valley. If a Huntsman issues an earnest challenge to a changeling by the fire for its safety or something else precious, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <b>Quenching the Fire:</b> Summer never yields its anger. If a Huntsman can erode at the Summer courtier's sense of anger, whether by instilling joy or sorrow, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn</b><br /> <b>Theater of Dreams:</b> The Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they manipulate the dreams of a changeling's mortal allies in order to draw out the changeling.<br /> <b>Solemn Vow:</b> Huntsmen excel at twisting the bonds between the Lost. The Huntsman gains a point of Yearning if it can manipulate the changeling or one of her allies into breaking a pledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Winter</b><br /> <b>Not All Who Wander are Lost:</b> The Huntsmen are masters of manipulation. When one uses a token of something a changeling lost to break her confidence, it gains a point of Yearning.<br /> <b>Frozen Heart:</b> Winter courtiers are often wreathed in sorrow as the land is wreathed in snow and ice. If a Huntsman can prey upon a changeling's sorrow and convince her to retreat into mournful solitude, it gains a point of Yearning.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much, Claire! Do you have any insight on what the Goblin Vows should target?<br /> <br /> Also, what does it mean when a universal contract, like Might of the Terrible Brute, is a court contract? If no one can speak to the latter, I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:33:15-08:00","id":836368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=836284#post836284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see the Seelie and Unseelie courts written up. They're mentioned briefly in Toronto but has anyone done a fan version yet?</div> </div> </div> </div> I assume its the Day/Night courts. Or maybe Dawn/Dusk. There's also a Seelie and Unseelie option in Rites of Spring for a Spring/Summer and Fall/Winter alliance. We could be talking either one of these.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:49:55-08:00","id":836373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=836368#post836368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I assume its the Day/Night courts. Or maybe Dawn/Dusk. There's also a Seelie and Unseelie option in Rites of Spring for a Spring/Summer and Fall/Winter alliance. We could be talking either one of these.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, dusk and dawn definitely aren't it, and I don't think day and night are either. We never has a proper look at them in 1e but at least we have court rules now to make our own if it doesn't happen officially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T06:05:36-08:00","id":836378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=836373#post836373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, dusk and dawn definitely aren't it, and I don't think day and night are either. We never has a proper look at them in 1e but at least we have court rules now to make our own if it doesn't happen officially.</div> </div> </div> </div> What makes you so sure its not Day/Night? Or the alliance I mentioned in RoS? You seem pretty sure about that. I mean, the Seelie and Unseelie myths come from the same regions as where the Seasonal and Day/Night Courts dominate. Seelie Court system is mentioned alongside Directional, but no mention of Day/Night, which would be an odd thing to drop considering they're placed together in the same book. The Seelie Court is called &quot;The Shining Throne,&quot; &quot;The Golden Ones&quot; and &quot;The Light Court&quot; in mythology, which matches the Day Court, while the Unseelie court are generally nocturnal, which again implies Night Court.<br /> <br /> A better question, perhaps, would be what is there about your idea of the Seelie and Unseelie that aren't being covered? The only defining feature between Seelie and Unseelie that I'm aware of is a division between &quot;light&quot; and &quot;dark&quot; with an emphasis on being more helpful to people in the day versus being more offensive at night time. How is this different from existing courts? What are the defining features that aren't already covered?<br /> <br /> EDIT - hells, there are some people that say that the Unseelie/Seelie divide is also the same divide between the Gentry and the Lost as well. The former are clearly uncaring about humans, while the latter are on the side of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-24-2016, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:39:36-08:00","id":836431,"title":"","content":"If you want to call a seasonal alliance or Day and Night courts the Seelie and Unseelie you can, but I think that Day and Night is too caught up in the literal 'It's daytime, we're in power for the next twelve hours' to be a good representative of the myths. Emotionally I could see an argument for Disgust fitting the Unseelie but Shame isn't what comes to mind when thinking of Seelie emotional possibilities. Court of the West's Honor would be a good seelie emotion, maybe. There's more than a literal brightness and light and happy sunshine to the seelie and there's more to darkness, nighttime, and evil to the unseelie. I think a proper write up would have to get into more of the subtle details. <br /> <br /> Mythology changes depending on the source, of course, but the Unseelie consider chaos as a natural state. Being changeable and adaptable help them survive, power unused is power wasted, and instinct and desire are things that should be acted on. In the seasonal alliance model Spring gets tossed in with the Seelie, but 'Desire' in the hands on powerful fae creatures who don't hesitate to use their power where their whims take them can be a very dark thing that produces the classical Unseelie disregard for humanity. On the Seelie side, we often see a strict code of honor, chivalry, and the exaltation of beautiful things. The Seelie are just as likely to snatch a human as the Unseelie- they're just more likely to set that person in a gilded cage to 'keep them safe' and fete them with parties, dancing, and gorgeous clothes while they're trapped. For their own good, of course. In game terms, the bias towards pretty could wind up with the Seelie being rather Seemingist though a hideous dwarf type changeling who can craft beautiful instruments or produce beauty in some other way also fits the ideal. The Unseelie take everyone though, and I could some changelings who might normally be Seelie by nature wind up going Unseelie simply because they don't like how Seemingist and shallow the Seelie can sometimes. <br /> <br /> Anyways, just spitballing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:47:00-08:00","id":836436,"title":"","content":"I have always thought that the traditional Seelie and Unseelie Courts were more closely aligned with the Gentry. I'd hazard a guess that if the Gentry get their heads out of their asses long enough to consider any form of society or philosophy, it'd be the Seelie/Unseelie Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T10:59:30-08:00","id":836532,"title":"","content":"Since each Court has an affinity contract, should it have an additional effect, like a Seeming bonus? That would go a long way to personalize and flavor up a court. I'd like having that, and it wouldnt be too hard homebrew a seasonal bonus for their single contract. Goblin Vow covers a LOT of ground now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T11:22:50-08:00","id":836547,"title":"","content":"Well that conversation seems familiar.<br /> <br /> If Court Affinity bonuses to Contracts aren't in the core, they'll certainly be in a supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T18:59:13-08:00","id":836795,"title":"","content":"A simple court contract Affinity bonus would be to add Mantle to Activation Rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:03:00-08:00","id":836798,"title":"","content":"Seriously, it's like there's an echo in time and space here. The writers just had this conversation, in this order, like, two days ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:16:52-08:00","id":836808,"title":"","content":"Great minds think alike?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T19:22:11-08:00","id":836810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=836798#post836798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, it's like there's an echo in time and space here. The writers just had this conversation, in this order, like, two days ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.thedoctorwhosite.co.uk/wp-images/doctorwho/themes/crack-cover.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:59:13-08:00","id":836991,"title":"","content":"I feel like the contract being cheaper or even free (if it's a set 2 dot contract) would also be appropriate. Maybe if you do that, let them use Mantle in place of Wyrd. If you want it to be even more ubiquitous but adding Mantle to the roll is too much, let them use mantle in place of one of their attribute, skill, or wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 02-25-2016, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:36:48-08:00","id":837160,"title":"","content":"I dunno, personally I like the idea of a unique seeming-like court affinity trick or power. Its more flavorful than just adding Mantle. The seeming bonuses arent just fun and flavorful, but it sneaks in some old contracts. I think itd be cool if courts had similar, to reflect some 1e signature powers the same way. And that is fairly entertaining that the devs had this very conversation XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:33:55-08:00","id":837193,"title":"","content":"I've started writing up the Seasonal Court of Buena Vista. I could use some help coming up with positions and offices. One 'cycle' I've got going is (class) of (season). Ziggy is the Sorcerer of Autumn, and I'm thinking he'd have counterparts in the Druid (or Bard?) of Spring, Knight of Summer, and Spymaster of Winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:38:07-08:00","id":837194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=836331#post836331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much, Claire! Do you have any insight on what the Goblin Vows should target?<br /> <br /> Also, what does it mean when a universal contract, like Might of the Terrible Brute, is a court contract? If no one can speak to the latter, I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not yet on the Goblin Vows. I'm still working on that, but I will be back to let you know when I figure it out. We also have Astrological Courts as a minor Court in the area, though they may rise to prominence.<br /> <br /> As Arc already pointed out, we've been discussing ideas on what to do with Court affinity Contracts. I am personally in favor of the Court affinities providing a bonus effect like Seeming affinities do. Even if it doesn't make it into a core, there's a good chance it'll see play in future books. And if not, well, I'm going to add them in my own games, and can share some ideas then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T14:00:55-08:00","id":837206,"title":"","content":"Yeah. One way or another, you guys are going to get Court 'Incepts'. It's just a matter of when.<br /> <br /> They will not be as terrifyingly powerful as Incepts, but you get the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T14:35:50-08:00","id":837223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/834478-2e-making-the-seasonal-courts-for-actual-play?p=837194#post837194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Arc already pointed out, we've been discussing ideas on what to do with Court affinity Contracts. I am personally in favor of the Court affinities providing a bonus effect like Seeming affinities do. Even if it doesn't make it into a core, there's a good chance it'll see play in future books. And if not, well, I'm going to add them in my own games, and can share some ideas then.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems so awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}